# Where the NAS is, from this Mac. Copy to deploy/deploy.env and set NAS_SSH.
#
# This file is about *reaching* the NAS. The server's own configuration —
# Firebase, Google, thresholds — lives in deploy/.env and is sent across with
# the deployment. Neither is committed.

# Required. Anything `ssh` understands: a host from ~/.ssh/config, a name on the
# local network, or an address.
NAS_SSH=pablo@nas.local

# The photo library on the NAS. Leave it unset the first time and run
# `./deploy/deploy.sh --check`: it will list the shared folders it can see and
# ask you to pick one.
# LIBRARY_PATH=/srv/dev-disk-by-uuid-xxxx/Photos

# Where the compose file, the ledger and the publishing folder live.
# Defaults: REMOTE_DIR=/srv/phototools, and data/ and publishing/ inside it.
# REMOTE_DIR=/srv/phototools
# DATA_PATH=/srv/phototools/data
# PUBLISHING_PATH=/srv/phototools/publishing

# What the container runs as. Unset means "whoever owns the library", which is
# what you want on OMV, where shared folders belong to a user the image has
# never heard of. Set these only to override that.
# PHOTOTOOLS_UID=1000
# PHOTOTOOLS_GID=100

# The NAS is x86-64, so the build cross-compiles from this ARM Mac. --check
# refuses to go on if this disagrees with what the NAS reports.
# PLATFORM=linux/amd64
